# Construction estimation agent

AI cost and material estimation agent for building a wood-frame house. Western market, US first.

## Stack

- `server/`: Node.js + Express
- `client/`: React + Vite + Tailwind + shadcn/ui
- Database: Supabase (PostgreSQL)
- LLM: OpenAI function calling

## Estimation boundary

The LLM never does arithmetic. All quantities and costs come from deterministic, tested functions in `server/src/estimators/`. The LLM only extracts inputs, calls tools, and explains results.

```javascript
// ❌ BAD — model invents a total
const total = await llm("What does 2400 sqft of framing cost?");

// ✅ GOOD — code computes; model only narrates
const result = estimateFraming({ sqft: 2400, rate });
```

Every estimate must include:

- The assumptions used
- A low/high range
- The disclaimer: `Budget estimate only. Not a bid or structural design.`

## Code

- Use ES modules and small pure functions.
- Write a vitest test for every estimator function.
- Keep rates, quantity factors, and percentages in the database. Do not hardcode them.

## Secrets

Never commit secrets. Use `.env` (gitignored) and `.env.example`.

Read docs/ARCHITECTURE.md before changing chat, agent, upload, estimate or export code, and keep it updated when the flow changes.
